%% scholar pipeline — the package's functions across three layers.
%% The connective tissue between layers is a paper's id (DOI/arXiv/PMID/PMCID/OpenAlex):
%% layer 1 and 2 emit records carrying ids, which are fed into layer 2 and 3 calls.
%% Render with any Mermaid viewer, or read top-to-bottom as an ordered message log.
sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant Driver as Claude (skill driver)
    participant Scholar as scholar package (the engine)
    participant Sources as Source libraries (pyalex, arxiv, habanero, biopython, semanticscholar, Europe PMC)
    participant Full as Full-text ladder (arXiv, PMC, Unpaywall, bioRxiv/medRxiv, CORE, Sci-Hub, Anna's Archive) + PyMuPDF

    User->>Driver: Natural-language query
    Driver->>Driver: Choose which functions to compose (broad by default)

    note over Driver,Sources: Layer 1 - find  (search)
    Driver->>Scholar: call search(query, ...)
    par Parallel fan-out
        Scholar->>Sources: query each source via its client library
        Sources-->>Scholar: normalized records, failures noted in meta
    end
    Scholar->>Scholar: de-duplicate (DOI and title) and rank
    Scholar-->>Driver: ranked results, each with ids (narrowing filters logged to stderr)

    note over Driver,Sources: Layer 2 - analyze  (lookup / citations / similar / facets / find_authors / coauthors / author_works)
    Driver->>Scholar: call a function with an id or author taken from a layer-1 record
    Scholar->>Sources: OpenAlex citation graph, facets, or author tally
    Sources-->>Scholar: related records (carrying more ids) or aggregate counts
    Scholar-->>Driver: results (any caveats logged to stderr)

    note over Driver,Full: Layer 3 - read  (fulltext / figures), only for the top papers that matter
    Driver->>Scholar: fulltext(download=True) or figures with a paper id
    Scholar->>Full: walk the open-access ladder, then Sci-Hub, then Anna's Archive, extract embedded figures with PyMuPDF
    Full-->>Scholar: the saved PDF path, or JPG figure images in a temp directory
    Scholar-->>Driver: pdf_path / image paths (Claude reads the PDF directly)

    Driver-->>User: Cited answer (title, authors, year, DOI, links) plus every relayed narrowing/exclusion
